WEBVTT

00:01.600 --> 00:04.789
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.814 --> 00:08.130
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.222 --> 00:11.291
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.341 --> 00:14.260
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.311 --> 00:18.180
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.265 --> 00:21.133
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.687 --> 00:23.221
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.336 --> 00:24.635
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.703 --> 00:30.017
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:37.731 --> 00:39.530
Good morning!

00:39.564 --> 00:41.399
Is what
normal families say.

00:41.467 --> 00:43.286
Lois, I'll take
my breakfast to go.

00:43.337 --> 00:44.953
I'm going fishing
with the fellas.

00:45.021 --> 00:46.655
Peter, I thought we
were going to have

00:46.722 --> 00:47.956
some family time
this weekend.

00:48.024 --> 00:49.256
You're going
fishing again?

00:49.323 --> 00:50.692
Yes, Lois. I love fishing.

00:50.760 --> 00:52.628
Remember, fishing was
my not-at-all-memorable job

00:52.695 --> 00:54.178
for two years?
- No.

00:54.245 --> 00:55.880
You don't remember
my fishing boat?

00:55.965 --> 00:57.416
You don't remember
Santos and Pasqual?

00:57.484 --> 00:58.665
Not even a little.

00:58.717 --> 00:59.985
They were like
male Consuelas.

01:00.052 --> 01:02.170
It was a mistake making 'em
Portuguese, though.

01:02.221 --> 01:04.053
People don't even know
what a Portuguese is.

01:04.121 --> 01:05.739
(chairs creaking)

01:05.807 --> 01:08.476
That's what I thought
a Portuguese was.

01:08.527 --> 01:10.778
Me and my brain, huh?

01:10.845 --> 01:12.747
And we're just
getting started!

01:12.816 --> 01:15.666
(birds squeaking,
foghorn blowing)

01:15.734 --> 01:18.569
Boy, it's not like Quagmire
to be this late.

01:18.653 --> 01:21.404
Yeah.

01:21.489 --> 01:22.857
<i>Jeez, I've never tried</i>

01:22.908 --> 01:24.576
<i>to make conversation
with just Joe before.</i>

01:24.660 --> 01:26.243
<i>This is brutal.</i>

01:26.311 --> 01:28.111
<i>Come on, Joe,
you're losing him.</i>

01:28.178 --> 01:29.346
<i>Think of something.</i>

01:29.414 --> 01:30.864
<i>This was your shot.</i>

01:30.932 --> 01:33.716
Two thirds
of the planet is water.

01:33.785 --> 01:35.336
Yeah.

01:35.387 --> 01:37.689
<i>Two thirds
of the planet is water?</i>

01:37.756 --> 01:39.807
<i>This guy's okay.</i>

01:39.874 --> 01:41.392
All right, well, um,

01:41.460 --> 01:43.727
we should probably go find out
what's keeping Quagmire.

01:43.795 --> 01:44.979
Yeah, I guess
you're right.

01:45.046 --> 01:46.865
And you know, Joe,
uh, I was thinking.

01:46.932 --> 01:49.400
Maybe one night we get
dinner, just the two of us.

01:49.467 --> 01:50.601
I would like that.

01:53.955 --> 01:55.154
(knocking)
PETER: Hey, Quagmire?

01:55.222 --> 01:57.157
You in there?

01:58.727 --> 02:00.394
(gasps)
Holy crap!

02:00.445 --> 02:01.780
Oh, my God!

02:01.863 --> 02:04.447
He must have autoerotically
asphyxiated himself!

02:04.515 --> 02:06.751
Yeah, while he was
watching clown porn.

02:06.819 --> 02:08.485
Oh, yeah, baby.

02:08.553 --> 02:11.089
Oh yeah, baby!
You make me so horny!

02:11.156 --> 02:12.239
(bicycle horn blowing)

02:12.289 --> 02:14.408
Come on, help me get him down!

02:18.729 --> 02:20.064
Peter, he's still alive!

02:20.131 --> 02:22.131
We got to get him
to a hospital!

02:22.199 --> 02:24.468
All right, but let's just watch
the end of this clown porn first.

02:24.536 --> 02:28.221
(calliope music playing)

02:31.943 --> 02:34.428
Oh, Peter, we came
as soon as we heard.

02:34.496 --> 02:35.628
How is he?

02:35.697 --> 02:37.163
He's in a coma, Lois.

02:37.232 --> 02:39.400
My God, what the hell happened?

02:39.451 --> 02:42.385
He hung himself during
autoerotic asphyxiation.

02:42.453 --> 02:44.520
Just goes to show anything
can be dangerous.

02:44.588 --> 02:46.223
Is his family here?

02:46.291 --> 02:48.542
His sister Brenda is coming
with her boyfriend, Jeff.

02:48.610 --> 02:50.194
Oh, my God, not that guy.

02:50.261 --> 02:51.778
Is she still with him?

02:51.845 --> 02:53.446
Isn't he the one
that beats her?

02:53.514 --> 02:54.947
Yeah, but she's
gotten a lot better.

02:57.550 --> 02:59.453
All right, on the way back,

02:59.521 --> 03:02.221
I get to pick the radio station,
because that was awful.

03:02.289 --> 03:04.757
I know, yeah, it
was, I'm sorry.

03:04.825 --> 03:06.692
Oh, God, I just...
I hope Glenn's okay.

03:06.760 --> 03:07.927
I'm so worried about him.

03:07.995 --> 03:09.362
Shut up and limp!

03:09.430 --> 03:10.964
We're in a handicapped spot,
you slut!

03:14.118 --> 03:15.652
Well, Miss Quagmire,

03:15.720 --> 03:17.252
your brother Glenn
is lucky to be alive.

03:17.321 --> 03:21.323
You know, we're all lucky to be
alive on such a beautiful day.

03:21.390 --> 03:24.260
In fact, nurse--
all surgeries are outside today.

03:24.328 --> 03:26.244
You know, when we were kids,

03:26.312 --> 03:28.731
our mother used to sing
a song when we were sad.

03:28.799 --> 03:30.351
Maybe that'll help now.

03:30.417 --> 03:32.652
Come on, Brenda,
a stupid nursery rhyme

03:32.720 --> 03:35.054
isn't going to wake him up,
especially the way you sing.

03:35.122 --> 03:36.338
(laughing)
Right, man?

03:36.406 --> 03:37.908
Gyaaaa.

03:37.976 --> 03:42.295
♪ Glenn, don't die from
autoerotic asphyxiation ♪

03:42.346 --> 03:45.432
♪ Your friends want to
go fishing with you... ♪

03:45.500 --> 03:46.999
This song is from childhood?

03:47.050 --> 03:53.056
♪ Live to see tomorrow,
October 31, 2011. ♪

03:55.776 --> 03:57.743
Where am I?

03:57.811 --> 03:58.778
What happened?

03:58.846 --> 04:00.146
Oh, Glenn!

04:00.214 --> 04:01.947
Oh, thank God
you're all right!

04:02.015 --> 04:03.498
Hey, you touching
my girl?!

04:03.567 --> 04:04.634
Relax, Jeff.
That's her brother.

04:04.701 --> 04:06.001
Yeah, that's how it starts.

04:06.068 --> 04:08.171
Come on, Brenda, we
got to get out of here.

04:08.238 --> 04:09.321
I need cigarettes
and jeans.

04:14.228 --> 04:16.496
Oh, thanks, you guys, for all
your help through this.

04:16.563 --> 04:19.165
Oh, Glenn, we're just
so glad you're all right.

04:19.216 --> 04:20.800
And Jeff and I are happy
to stay here with you

04:20.867 --> 04:22.468
for as long as you need.

04:22.536 --> 04:24.587
Fine, then you call
my cousin Terry

04:24.655 --> 04:27.006
and tell him we're not going
to be at his karate recital!

04:27.074 --> 04:28.875
Well, Jeff,
he is my brother.

04:28.941 --> 04:31.543
Why do you always got to remind
me I didn't finish high school?

04:31.612 --> 04:35.181
Well, listen, how about I make
us all some dinner, huh?

04:35.248 --> 04:36.348
Come here!

04:37.601 --> 04:38.701
(clattering)

04:38.768 --> 04:40.069
You fat, ugly bitch!

04:40.137 --> 04:41.703
If today
wasn't your birthday...

04:41.772 --> 04:43.371
Jeff! Please,
you're being...

04:43.439 --> 04:44.874
What?!
What am I being?!

04:44.942 --> 04:46.308
Crazy?!
Unemployed?!

04:46.375 --> 04:48.678
Why don't you call the cops
like you did on Christmas?!

04:48.745 --> 04:50.811
I-I-I didn't call them!
They were called!

04:50.879 --> 04:53.749
Oh, now you're calling me a liar
in front of this cat?!

04:53.817 --> 04:54.983
I got another cat.

05:00.679 --> 05:03.348
Aw, that yellow lab
looks like it's dying.

05:03.381 --> 05:04.616
Peter,
that's Gwyneth Paltrow.

05:04.684 --> 05:05.783
She's fine.

05:05.850 --> 05:07.467
Look, turn off the light.

05:07.534 --> 05:10.237
I just want to get to sleep and
put this ugly night behind us.

05:10.305 --> 05:12.673
All that unpleasantness
with Brenda and Jeff

05:12.741 --> 05:13.975
was more than I can handle.

05:14.043 --> 05:15.475
It's no big deal, Lois.

05:15.542 --> 05:16.933
We probably just caught
'em on an off night.

05:16.934 --> 05:18.395
JEFF: Where do you get
off calling me a deadbeat

05:18.419 --> 05:19.620
in front of your brother?!

05:20.230 --> 05:22.601
BRENDA: No, Jeff, a-a-all I said was
that you were in between jobs!

05:22.667 --> 05:24.501
JEFF:
Well, it wouldn't matter

05:24.568 --> 05:26.103
if you'd just pick up that
night shift at the prison!

05:26.171 --> 05:28.640
BRENDA: But then I'll be working
a hundred hours a week.

05:28.708 --> 05:29.857
JEFF:
So what?!

05:29.908 --> 05:32.359
I need money for motor oil
and wallet chains!

05:32.410 --> 05:34.661
BRENDA:
Okay, I'll ask about it Monday.

05:34.729 --> 05:36.229
Can I put my nightgown
back on?

05:36.281 --> 05:38.650
JEFF:
No, I'm not done drawing!

05:40.669 --> 05:41.602
(doorbell rings)

05:45.557 --> 05:47.624
Hey, Peter.

05:47.692 --> 05:49.425
Geez, Quagmire,
you look terrible.

05:49.493 --> 05:52.013
Oh, I didn't get any sleep.

05:52.081 --> 05:53.281
Hi, Glenn.
How are you?

05:53.349 --> 05:54.714
Not great, Lois.

05:54.782 --> 05:57.134
I'm stuck in the middle of some
bad stuff with my sister.

05:57.218 --> 05:59.553
I know, it sounded like there
was quite a ruckus going on

05:59.621 --> 06:01.256
over there last night.

06:01.324 --> 06:03.007
That Jeff seems like
kind of a monster.

06:03.074 --> 06:05.342
Yeah, that guy's scary
as an Iraq Lobster.

06:05.410 --> 06:08.262
(playing "Rock Lobster")

06:10.898 --> 06:12.198
♪ Death to America ♪

06:13.703 --> 06:14.935
♪ And butter sauce ♪

06:16.154 --> 06:17.304
♪ Don't boil me ♪

06:18.740 --> 06:20.907
♪ I'm still alive ♪

06:20.976 --> 06:22.209
♪ Iraq Lobster ♪

06:26.080 --> 06:28.148
♪ Iraq Lobster. ♪

06:32.019 --> 06:34.353
I've tried talking to Brenda
about leaving him,

06:34.420 --> 06:36.023
but I haven't
gotten anywhere.

06:36.090 --> 06:38.158
I was actually hoping
you could talk to her, Lois.

06:38.227 --> 06:40.894
She might open up more to you,
you know, 'cause you're a woman.

06:40.962 --> 06:43.496
- Me?
- Yeah, would you mind at least trying?

06:43.564 --> 06:45.966
Well, I guess she does
need someone to talk to.

06:46.034 --> 06:47.485
Well, let's hope
she's good at talking

06:47.553 --> 06:49.335
'cause we know she doesn't
listen so good.

06:49.403 --> 06:50.837
That... we know.

06:53.540 --> 06:55.875
You know, Brenda, I'm glad
we could get together.

06:55.943 --> 06:57.176
Me, too, Lois.

06:57.244 --> 06:59.044
It's nice to have a
girlfriend to chat with.

06:59.112 --> 07:00.513
Don't you have any
back home?

07:00.581 --> 07:02.549
Oh, no. Jeff would
never allow that.

07:02.617 --> 07:03.999
You know, that's kind of what

07:04.067 --> 07:05.868
I want to talk to you about,
Brenda.

07:05.936 --> 07:07.471
Do you mind
taking off your sunglasses?

07:10.224 --> 07:11.657
Oh, my God.

07:11.725 --> 07:13.526
No, i-it's really
not that bad.

07:13.594 --> 07:15.128
It only hurts when I see.

07:15.196 --> 07:16.797
You know, you don't have
to stay with a man

07:16.865 --> 07:18.263
who treats you that way.

07:18.331 --> 07:20.283
Oh, Jeff's sweet.

07:20.350 --> 07:23.118
You don't see how soft and gentle
he hits me when we're alone.

07:23.186 --> 07:24.555
Do you hear yourself?

07:24.621 --> 07:26.289
He shouldn't be
hitting you at all.

07:26.356 --> 07:28.758
I don't think you understand
how serious a matter...

07:28.826 --> 07:30.276
Close your menu.
What?

07:30.344 --> 07:32.361
Close your menu, so they
know we're ready to order.

07:32.429 --> 07:33.612
I'll give you
another moment.

07:33.680 --> 07:34.897
Damn it.

07:34.966 --> 07:37.650
I'm sorry.
Oh, shoot.

07:37.717 --> 07:39.652
See, this is why Jeff
corrects me all the time.

07:39.720 --> 07:41.137
Corrects you?

07:41.205 --> 07:43.472
Brenda, he's not correcting you,
he's beating you!

07:43.539 --> 07:46.075
Well, I-I-I can see
why you'd think that

07:46.143 --> 07:47.808
'cause of the punches and all,

07:47.877 --> 07:50.446
but it's just that Jeff's been
so angry about immigrants.

07:50.514 --> 07:51.782
What?!

07:51.850 --> 07:53.882
It'll be better when
he gets back to work.

07:53.950 --> 07:55.902
Our relationship is just
complicated, that's all.

07:55.969 --> 07:58.337
No, Brenda,
it's not complicated.

07:58.405 --> 07:59.806
Trying to get
a straight answer

07:59.873 --> 08:02.042
out of a 23-year-old
girl is complicated.

08:02.109 --> 08:03.926
So, do you want
to go out some time?

08:03.994 --> 08:06.362
Out like, go out or hang out
or just do something?

08:06.430 --> 08:07.663
Like a date.

08:07.730 --> 08:09.098
Like a date date?
Or like a date?

08:09.166 --> 08:10.816
Both, I... I guess.

08:10.883 --> 08:12.734
Yeah, sure, maybe.
I don't know. Yes, no.

08:12.819 --> 08:14.520
Here's the first three
digits of my phone number.

08:14.588 --> 08:16.089
E-mail me.

08:19.258 --> 08:20.526
Joe, the guy's a menace.

08:20.594 --> 08:22.410
They've been with me
three days now,

08:22.478 --> 08:24.713
and all he does is beat her
day and night.

08:24.781 --> 08:26.365
And on top of that,
they say they don't need

08:26.416 --> 08:27.916
to be entertained,
but then they're always like,

08:27.984 --> 08:29.367
"Hey, so what're we doing?
What's next?"

08:29.418 --> 08:31.370
Hey, Joe, can't you...
can't you just arrest the guy?

08:31.421 --> 08:33.021
I can't arrest Jeff

08:33.089 --> 08:35.590
unless Brenda files a formal
complaint with the police.

08:35.659 --> 08:36.892
She won't go to the police.

08:36.959 --> 08:39.061
She's afraid
of what Jeff will do.

08:39.129 --> 08:40.428
And to be honest,
I don't blame her.

08:40.496 --> 08:42.280
I mean, w-w-what happens
if one of these nights,

08:42.348 --> 08:43.615
he hits her so hard
he kills her?

08:43.683 --> 08:45.083
Sorry, Quagmire.

08:45.150 --> 08:48.321
Police policy, we can't step
in until it's too late.

08:48.388 --> 08:50.456
But if I were you, I'd
set up an intervention.

08:50.524 --> 08:51.690
What's that?

08:51.757 --> 08:53.493
It's like a surprise
birthday party,

08:53.559 --> 08:56.395
but instead of cake and
presents, there's angry letters

08:56.463 --> 08:57.696
and someone who
inappropriately tries

08:57.763 --> 08:59.030
to make it about themselves.

08:59.098 --> 09:00.600
Aw, that sounds great!

09:00.667 --> 09:02.399
I bet I would really shine
at one of those.

09:05.171 --> 09:07.372
All right, well, first
we want to thank you all

09:07.440 --> 09:09.040
for being here for Brenda.

09:09.108 --> 09:10.909
Now, I know it's going
to be a long day,

09:10.977 --> 09:14.196
but we're all here because we
care about her very much.

09:14.263 --> 09:15.697
What the... what's going on?

09:15.765 --> 09:16.948
What's all this?

09:16.999 --> 09:18.883
Brenda, this is
an intervention.

09:18.950 --> 09:21.253
A lot of us don't like how
Jeff's been treating you.

09:21.320 --> 09:23.055
So we're going
to say a few things,

09:23.122 --> 09:25.491
and then you'll say a few
things, and then we'll be done.

09:25.559 --> 09:26.657
Sound good?

09:26.725 --> 09:28.126
Um...
I guess.

09:28.193 --> 09:30.897
All right, so we're going to go
around the room and tell you

09:30.963 --> 09:33.081
exactly how your situation
has affected each of us.

09:33.149 --> 09:34.583
Meg?

09:34.650 --> 09:38.019
I feel like if he likes you,
maybe you can change him.

09:38.087 --> 09:39.521
Okay, maybe she wasn't
the one to start with.

09:39.589 --> 09:40.673
Caleb?

09:43.508 --> 09:45.845
Caleb, you want
to go ahead?

09:45.911 --> 09:47.496
M... M... me?

09:47.563 --> 09:48.562
Yeah, go ahead.

09:48.630 --> 09:50.882
Uh... It's Chris.

09:50.949 --> 09:52.517
Y-You don't know my name?

09:52.585 --> 09:54.351
All right, this isn't off
to a flying start.

09:54.419 --> 09:55.953
Peter, why don't you go ahead?

09:56.020 --> 09:58.123
So, you like
getting beaten, huh?

09:58.191 --> 10:00.392
Well, why don't you smoke a
whole carton of cigarettes!

10:00.459 --> 10:02.210
Look, I know what you guys
are trying to do,

10:02.295 --> 10:03.761
but Jeff and I are fine.

10:03.828 --> 10:06.297
No, Brenda,
you're not fine, okay?

10:06.364 --> 10:08.682
Please, I'd like to say
something, if I may.

10:08.750 --> 10:10.051
(clearing throat)

10:10.119 --> 10:14.005
"Brenda, the fact that
you are being abused

10:14.056 --> 10:16.725
"has affected my life
in the following ways:

10:16.809 --> 10:19.511
"The sister that I knew
and loved growing up

10:19.563 --> 10:22.030
"no longer exists.

10:22.114 --> 10:25.649
"The person I see before me now
is just a punching bag.

10:25.700 --> 10:28.787
"And I call you 'person'
and not 'woman'

10:28.854 --> 10:31.873
"because a woman is a strong,
beautiful, vibrant creature.

10:31.958 --> 10:34.326
"A woman embraces life.

10:34.377 --> 10:37.062
"A woman makes choices
to make her life better.

10:37.129 --> 10:41.366
"Sadly, the fact that you are
with Jeff, proves to me

10:41.434 --> 10:45.868
that you have made a choice
to make your life worse."

10:45.936 --> 10:48.505
I-I want the girl
I grew up with back.

10:48.573 --> 10:52.927
I want... I want my sister back.

10:53.011 --> 10:56.230
Brenda, I love you.

10:56.314 --> 10:58.333
Please make the right decision.

10:58.401 --> 11:00.267
Which is a perfect time
for me to tell my jokes.

11:00.351 --> 11:01.552
Peter!

11:01.604 --> 11:02.987
And I will save
them for the end.

11:06.558 --> 11:09.261
Glenn, I am so lucky

11:09.328 --> 11:13.029
to have such a wonderful,
loving brother like you.

11:17.502 --> 11:20.369
So, are you gonna
leave him?

11:20.420 --> 11:22.539
Oh, there you are!

11:22.590 --> 11:25.091
Hey, give me some money!
I saw a cool bandana.

11:25.159 --> 11:26.860
What the hell's going on here?!

11:26.928 --> 11:29.096
Listen here, you bully!
For your information,

11:29.165 --> 11:30.464
Brenda just agreed
to leave you!

11:30.531 --> 11:32.082
Like hell she did.

11:32.150 --> 11:33.116
Brenda, you tell 'em?

11:33.184 --> 11:34.617
No, not yet.

11:34.686 --> 11:37.353
Everyone...
I have wonderful news.

11:37.421 --> 11:39.822
Jeff and I are getting married.

11:39.890 --> 11:40.958
(all gasp)

11:41.026 --> 11:42.308
I'd show you the ring,

11:42.376 --> 11:43.928
but it's under the splint.

11:43.995 --> 11:45.695
My finger fell down the stairs.

11:45.764 --> 11:47.264
You're getting married?!

11:47.332 --> 11:49.148
Yeah, but only 'cause
she's pregnant.

11:49.233 --> 11:50.333
Pregnant?!

11:50.402 --> 11:52.752
Oh, congratulations!

11:52.820 --> 11:54.437
Have you thought
of any names yet?

11:54.505 --> 11:56.240
Maybe... maybe
"Slappy"?

11:56.308 --> 11:57.740
Or-or "Bruisey"?

11:57.809 --> 11:59.475
Or "Keep-It-Down-
In-There-sy"?

12:05.151 --> 12:07.053
Guys, what the hell
am I gonna do?

12:07.097 --> 12:08.232
She can't marry
that bastard.

12:08.299 --> 12:09.698
He's just gonna
keep beatin' her,

12:09.766 --> 12:11.634
and then he's gonna beat
the kid, too!

12:11.703 --> 12:14.138
God, I wish she'd never met
Jeffrey Fecalman.

12:14.205 --> 12:15.973
You know, I was
thinking... Wait, what?

12:16.040 --> 12:17.574
What?
That's his name?

12:17.642 --> 12:19.474
Yeah.
Huh-larious.

12:19.542 --> 12:21.210
But you know,
I was thinking this afternoon,

12:21.278 --> 12:23.547
what the hell happened to the
days when a guy does something

12:23.615 --> 12:26.899
like that to a girl, and a bunch
of us guys get together

12:26.967 --> 12:29.368
and just go kick
his (bleep) ass?

12:29.436 --> 12:31.336
Boy, that'd be
satisfying.

12:31.405 --> 12:33.440
Well... why not?

12:33.508 --> 12:34.606
What do you mean?

12:34.674 --> 12:35.942
The three of us.

12:36.009 --> 12:37.878
We go over there
and we do what's right;

12:37.946 --> 12:38.977
we kill the bastard.

12:39.045 --> 12:40.545
Whoa, whoa, Quagmire.

12:40.614 --> 12:42.916
You know, I could arrest
you just for saying that.

12:42.984 --> 12:44.282
You know what else
you can get arrested for?

12:44.351 --> 12:45.585
Soliciting a rooster.

12:45.652 --> 12:48.721
I don't know what this
cock-a-doodle-doo thing is,

12:48.789 --> 12:50.990
but it sounds gay
and it sounds scatological.

12:51.058 --> 12:52.626
I'm in.

12:52.694 --> 12:54.894
You're about to
have a neat day.

12:54.962 --> 12:56.997
Quagmire, you're talking
about murdering a guy.

12:57.065 --> 12:58.263
It doesn't matter

12:58.331 --> 13:00.266
what he's done,
it's still murder.

13:00.335 --> 13:02.068
<i>No, Joe, it does matter
what he's done!</i>

13:02.136 --> 13:04.103
These kinds of guys
don't change.

13:04.170 --> 13:06.573
Y-you think they ever suddenly
wake up and realize

13:06.641 --> 13:09.275
the error of their ways
and clean up their act? No!

13:09.359 --> 13:10.793
They just keep ruining
everyone's lives,

13:10.862 --> 13:12.713
and the world is better off
without 'em.

13:12.780 --> 13:14.180
It's against the
law, Quagmire,

13:14.249 --> 13:15.348
and that's the
end of it.

13:15.415 --> 13:18.451
(loud slap, Brenda screams)

13:18.518 --> 13:19.986
JEFF: What the hell?!
Did you change the channel

13:20.054 --> 13:21.554
while I was going
to get a beer?!

13:21.623 --> 13:23.621
Oh, yeah, I-I'm sorry,
honey, I just wanted

13:23.688 --> 13:24.874
<i>to see who was
on Letterman.</i>

13:24.942 --> 13:26.476
<i>We're watching Leno,
you bitch!</i>

13:26.544 --> 13:27.728
I'm so sorry!

13:27.793 --> 13:30.029
His soft, gentle humor
connects effortlessly

13:30.097 --> 13:32.382
with my mainstream
sensibilities!

13:32.450 --> 13:33.448
(slaps)
(screams)

13:34.617 --> 13:36.385
Let's waste this dick.

13:37.987 --> 13:40.189
Boy, everything's different now
than it used to be, isn't it?

13:40.257 --> 13:42.791
You know, this morning I had
a bowl of Fruity Pebbles cereal.

13:42.860 --> 13:44.827
Yeah, yeah. When I was a kid,
they were boulders!

13:44.895 --> 13:47.864
(laughs loudly)

13:47.931 --> 13:49.298
(laughs)

13:49.366 --> 13:51.517
Cereals do change.

13:51.585 --> 13:52.868
Oh, no, no. Here's something,
here's something.

13:52.935 --> 13:54.053
Did you hear about this?

13:54.121 --> 13:55.637
Here's a bunch
of words in a row:

13:55.705 --> 13:57.274
because the economy's so bad,

13:57.340 --> 13:58.959
they've decided they're gonna
shut down all the prisons.

13:59.026 --> 14:00.560
Yeah, yeah.

14:00.626 --> 14:03.428
And-and they're gonna send
all the inmates to Congress.

14:03.496 --> 14:05.647
I don't get that one!

14:09.686 --> 14:11.153
Hi, there, Jeff.

14:11.222 --> 14:12.754
Hey, what's going
on, dudes?

14:12.805 --> 14:14.222
Brenda just fell.

14:14.291 --> 14:17.292
Get your lazy ass up and get
my neighbors some beers!

14:17.360 --> 14:19.094
Actually, we don't
have time, Jeff.

14:19.161 --> 14:20.929
We were just about
to go on

14:20.997 --> 14:22.663
our annual midnight
hunting trip.

14:22.731 --> 14:24.533
We thought you might
want to join us.

14:24.600 --> 14:25.868
Yeah, what the hell.

14:25.936 --> 14:28.570
Go shoot some animals,
that sounds like fun.

14:28.638 --> 14:30.974
Hey, it beats sitting at home
watching Meg pop her zits.

14:37.547 --> 14:39.264
(squish)

14:42.534 --> 14:44.569
Okay, okay,
who would you rather do?

14:44.637 --> 14:47.005
Dame Judi Dench with 30 minutes
of kissing first

14:47.072 --> 14:50.810
or Eddie Izzard in drag,
but he has a working vagina?

14:50.877 --> 14:52.812
Would Eddie Izzard tell
others about it?

14:52.879 --> 14:54.563
Eddie Izzard is very discreet.

14:54.630 --> 14:55.798
Then that's your answer.

14:55.866 --> 14:57.882
You know, Quagmire,
I gotta say,

14:57.950 --> 14:59.968
I was pretty surprised
you wanted me to come along.

15:00.036 --> 15:01.903
I thought
you hated my guts.

15:01.971 --> 15:03.288
(chuckles)
Oh, come on, Jeff,

15:03.356 --> 15:04.889
I don't hate your
(bleep) guts.

15:04.957 --> 15:06.325
Well, then what the hell
are we doing out here?

15:06.409 --> 15:08.010
I thought we were gonna kill...
Ah!

15:08.078 --> 15:10.946
So, Jeff, do you
like loud sentences?!

15:11.014 --> 15:11.929
I guess.

15:11.997 --> 15:14.165
I gotta take a whiz.

15:14.233 --> 15:15.850
All right, look,
when he comes back,

15:15.918 --> 15:17.535
I'm just gonna
do it, okay?

15:17.603 --> 15:19.553
I'm just gonna point my gun
straight at his head

15:19.622 --> 15:20.922
before he even knows
what's going on.

15:20.990 --> 15:21.922
(shotgun racks)

15:21.990 --> 15:23.592
Kinda like this?

15:23.659 --> 15:26.110
You know, Quagmire,
you are pathetic.

15:26.177 --> 15:28.247
You have to bring
your friends out here with you

15:28.315 --> 15:29.714
to do your dirty work?

15:29.782 --> 15:32.082
What... what do you mean, Jeff?

15:32.150 --> 15:33.784
You're gonna kill me,
is that it?

15:35.689 --> 15:37.788
Uh-uh!

15:37.856 --> 15:39.024
Not unless you want

15:39.091 --> 15:40.924
your friend's brains
all over the place!

15:41.009 --> 15:43.295
Listen, Jeff,
just put the gun down

15:43.362 --> 15:45.197
and we'll forget this whole
thing, okay?

15:47.583 --> 15:51.285
Oh. Well, that's never
happened before.

15:51.353 --> 15:53.622
Kinda don't know
what to do next.

15:53.689 --> 15:55.423
So now you'll forget
the whole thing?

15:55.491 --> 15:57.592
Yeah, I, uh, guess
that is what I said.

15:57.660 --> 15:59.243
No, no, we can't forget
the whole thing!

15:59.327 --> 16:00.578
Yeah, you know,
he's right.

16:00.662 --> 16:01.662
We can't forget it.

16:01.729 --> 16:03.581
Fine. Now here's
the plan:

16:03.666 --> 16:06.083
I'm taking Quagmire
for a little ride,

16:06.167 --> 16:09.304
and you guys are gonna stay out
here and freeze to death!

16:09.372 --> 16:11.372
Now, get those hands
where I can see 'em!

16:11.439 --> 16:13.791
All the way up!

16:13.876 --> 16:16.259
Oh, my shirt's a
little too short.

16:16.328 --> 16:17.494
That's okay.
You can keep 'em

16:17.563 --> 16:19.980
the way you had 'em
so it covers your stomach.

16:20.049 --> 16:22.516
<i>Thank you. You know, if
this Jeff was around more,</i>

16:22.584 --> 16:24.101
we wouldn't have
tried to kill you.

16:24.169 --> 16:25.220
See you later,
schmucks!

16:38.482 --> 16:40.266
All right,
this is far enough.

16:50.294 --> 16:53.013
Well, Quagmire, sorry
it had to end this way;

16:53.081 --> 16:55.215
a tragic hunting accident.

16:55.283 --> 16:58.017
I guess that little baby's gonna
grow up without an uncle.

16:58.085 --> 16:59.453
Actually,
I have a brother.

16:59.522 --> 17:01.155
Gary Quagmire.
Oh.

17:01.221 --> 17:03.675
I think... I think you got
a brother, too, don't you?

17:03.743 --> 17:04.941
All right, forget
the uncle thing!

17:05.009 --> 17:07.578
Get ready to die,
Quagmire.

17:07.645 --> 17:09.313
You know, if you had any balls,

17:09.382 --> 17:11.632
you'd put that gun down and we
could settle this like men.

17:11.699 --> 17:13.199
(laughs)

17:13.267 --> 17:16.353
That's awful big talk for a
scrawny bastard like you.

17:16.420 --> 17:17.721
Hey, I'm serious, man.

17:17.789 --> 17:19.522
Unless you're scared
I can take you.

17:19.590 --> 17:21.742
Suit yourself, man.

17:21.810 --> 17:24.328
Just means
you're gonna die slower.

17:42.280 --> 17:43.398
(spits)

17:47.035 --> 17:48.969
(bones crack)

17:51.004 --> 17:52.639
(gasping)

18:07.989 --> 18:09.205
(groans)

18:34.565 --> 18:35.798
(engine starts)

18:37.252 --> 18:38.383
(engine revs)

18:40.154 --> 18:42.021
What the hell?!
I killed you!

18:43.473 --> 18:46.159
I choke myself every day,
you bastard!

18:47.061 --> 18:48.661
(tires squeal)

18:59.005 --> 19:01.173
(radiator hissing)

19:15.706 --> 19:17.906
(sobbing)

19:19.560 --> 19:21.409
Oh, oh, Glenn,
there you are.

19:21.477 --> 19:24.614
Jeff didn't come home last night
and he hasn't called.

19:24.680 --> 19:26.381
Uh, well, actually,
about that, Brenda,

19:26.449 --> 19:28.416
he must've left
early this morning.

19:28.484 --> 19:30.936
Yeah, we found this
note he left you.

19:31.003 --> 19:34.207
"Dear Brenda,
I have decided to leave you.

19:34.274 --> 19:36.376
"I realized
that you are too good for me,

19:36.444 --> 19:38.643
"and you and our unborn child
would be better off

19:38.711 --> 19:41.112
"without me in the picture.
Love, Jeff.

19:41.180 --> 19:43.582
"P.S. If the cops ask, tell them

19:43.649 --> 19:46.352
"that Joe, Peter and Quagmire
were with you last night.

19:46.420 --> 19:47.986
"If you tell anyone otherwise,

19:48.054 --> 19:51.324
"I will come back and not only
hit you, but I will murder you.

19:51.391 --> 19:53.457
"And no one will care
because you're garbage.

19:53.525 --> 19:56.229
And your baby is going
to be a child of garbage."

19:56.296 --> 19:57.462
(hushed):
It's a little rough, Peter.

19:57.530 --> 19:58.965
I didn't write it. Joe did.

19:59.032 --> 20:00.398
I wanted it
to sound real.

20:00.466 --> 20:02.068
It's gotta sound
like he wrote it.

20:02.135 --> 20:04.170
Plus, she kinda is
garbage, Quagmire.

20:04.237 --> 20:06.672
"Well, I best be
rolling on now."

20:06.740 --> 20:08.708
(hushed): Oh, come on!
Who says that?!

20:08.775 --> 20:09.875
(hushed):
It's an expression.

20:09.943 --> 20:10.877
Yeah, if you're in
a wheelchair.

20:10.944 --> 20:11.910
Listen, you had
your chance.

20:11.978 --> 20:13.412
I e-mailed it
to both of you.

20:13.479 --> 20:14.713
You wrote back:
"Looks fine."

20:14.780 --> 20:16.598
And you just added that
part about Grape Ape.

20:16.666 --> 20:19.468
"P.P.S. I really love Grape Ape.

20:19.535 --> 20:20.502
The end."

20:20.570 --> 20:22.604
(sighs) Wow.

20:22.672 --> 20:25.006
I guess he's really gone.
(sobbing)

20:32.480 --> 20:34.182
I kinda want to kill
somebody else now.

20:34.250 --> 20:35.283
Ooh, Mort!

20:35.284 --> 21:36.284
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru